---
title: "Prepare a device and NAHPU"
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Prepare the installation, power, and essential settings before fieldwork.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Install or update NAHPU while reliable internet is available.
2. Charge the device and power banks, then confirm enough free storage.
3. Open `Setup NAHPU` from the home screen or the menu drawer and run the setup wizard.
4. Work through `Catalog format`, `Identifiers`, and the `Sites`, `Events`, `Specimens`, and `Parasites` vocabulary steps, or select `Import user configs` to reuse the setup your team already exported.
5. Test the camera, GPS, file picker, and intended backup destination.
6. Run one mock catalog session and correct the setup before departure.
{% /steps %}

{% aside type="tip" %}

Finish the wizard with `Export user configs` so every device on the team starts from the same setup.

{% /aside %}

